## 8. Where are installed applications stored?

When AppMan installs an application, it does not simply put one `.AppImage` file into your Applications directory.

It creates a dedicated directory for the application.

For example, a Google Chrome installation might have a structure similar to:

```
~/Applications/
│
└── google-chrome/
    │
    ├── google-chrome
    ├── AM-updater
    ├── remove
    │
    └── icons/
        └── google-chrome.png
```

It also creates integration files:

```
~/.local/bin/
└── google-chrome

~/.local/share/applications/
└── google-chrome-AM.desktop
```

Here is what each component does:

| File or directory              | Purpose                            |
| ------------------------------ | ---------------------------------- |
| `google-chrome/`               | Main application directory         |
| `google-chrome`                | Application executable or AppImage |
| `AM-updater`                   | Application update helper          |
| `remove`                       | Application removal script         |
| `icons/`                       | Application icons                  |
| `~/.local/bin/`                | Command-line launcher              |
| `~/.local/share/applications/` | Desktop application launcher       |

The exact files depend on the application and its installation script.

