## 21. My recommendations for your Ubuntu setup

Considering your goal of keeping portable applications separate from the Ubuntu system, I recommend this arrangement:

```
Ubuntu SSD
│
├── Ubuntu operating system
├── Home directory
├── AppMan executable
│   └── ~/.local/bin/appman
│
└── Application integration
    ├── ~/.local/bin/
    └── ~/.local/share/applications/

Dedicated Applications storage
│
└── Applications/
    ├── GoogleChrome/
    ├── Firefox/
    ├── SublimeText/
    ├── SublimeMerge/
    ├── Cursor/
    └── OtherApplications/
```

Keep AppMan's configuration, launchers, and command-line integration in your home directory. Store the actual applications on your chosen data drive.

One important precaution: because applications stored on another drive depend on that drive being mounted, make sure it mounts automatically before relying on those applications.

The three most important commands to remember are:

```
appman -ia APPLICATION_NAME  # Install AppImage
appman -u                   # Update applications
appman relocate             # Move AppMan applications
```

You can use `appman -h` whenever you need to inspect the available commands.

Documentation note: AppMan's official documentation is continuously updated. The command reference above is based on its documented interface; check the official repository if a particular option behaves differently in your installed version.</md></sn>
